  "guid": "com.matsix.fsr4bridge",
  "name": "FSR4 Bridge",
  "slug": "fsr4-bridge",
  "teaser": "Implements native FSR4 upscaler support",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/Oe0KxBW3g6ytcpUOEUvV63Z6clMP4TRfBvgVIPwi.png",
  "downloads": 1604,
  "favourites_count": 10,
  "description": "<h1>FSR4 Bridge - AMD FSR4 for SPT</h1>\n<p>Routes the game’s FSR3 upscaler to <strong>AMD FSR4</strong> (or the latest <strong>FSR 3.1.x</strong> as a fallback) via a\nnative D3D11 -&gt; D3D12 bridge. This is built using the latest FSR SDK, so it supports FSR 4.1.1 which works with RDNA3.</p>\n<p>If your card does not support FSR4 and you select it, it will auto fallback to 3.1.x.</p>\n<p><strong>NOTE: Keep in mind, this is a <em>bridge</em>, which means it needs to convert dx11 output to dx12 and back to dx11. It is extra processing power to do, on top of FSR4 itself being heavier in general. You may notice performance drop compared to FSR3.0 especially if you are using an RDNA3 card</strong></p>\n<h2>How to Use</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In the game’s <strong>Graphics</strong> settings, select an <strong>FSR3</strong> quality mode</li>\n<li>In the BepInEx <strong>config</strong> (F12 ConfigurationManager, or edit\n<code>BepInEx/config/com.matsix.fsr4bridge.cfg</code>), set <strong>Enable FSR4 = true</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>BepInEx Config</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Enable FSR4</strong> - the master toggle.</li>\n<li><strong>Sharpness</strong> (0–1) - RCAS post-sharpen. FSR4 is smoother than FSR3 by design (bypassing the game’s\nown FSR3 sharpen pass too), so raise this (~0.6–0.9) if edges look soft.</li>\n<li><strong>Native AA</strong> - Toggle between native resolution AA and upscaled AA</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>SPT-VR Support</h2>\n<p>You will need to be on version 1.3.1+ of SPT-VR for this bridge to work (will be available soon). I had to add special support for the VR mod since it changes\na lot of upscaler code.</p>\n<h2>Credits</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>AMD Fidelity FX SDK - <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://gpuopen.com/amd-fidelityfx-sdk/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://gpuopen.com/amd-fidelityfx-sdk/</a></li>\n<li>Claude for a lot of the bridge logic</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can support my work on Ko-fi:\n<a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/matsix\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://ko-fi.com/matsix</a></p>\n",
