    {
      "id": 14019,
      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "1.0.1",
      "description": "<p>Changelog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes a TDR caused when enabling/disabling settings in bepinex config</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Regarding performance - this is not a complete direct FSR4 implementation because that’s not possible due to Tarkov being DX11 and FSR4 does not support DX11. So this is doing the same thing optiscaler does pretty much except built into Tarkov directly to work best with Tarkov. This converts DX11 output to DX12 and back to DX11 so it needs to do extra processing. RDNA3 cards, I imagine would have an even harder time with this.</strong></p>\n<p>Another thing to note - if you’re testing performance in hideout, that is not a good representation. After a lot of testing, enabling this mod costs about 0.5ms frametime on my 9070 xt (on flatscreen). So the higher your FPS is, the bigger of a drop you’ll see. Go into a raid, look towards the middle of the map and enable/disable and see if it affects FPS. Let me know if you’re still seeing big drops in those cases.</p>\n",
